Q: Disable Submit button *after* jquery.validation A: <p>I think this should be a better way.</p>
<pre class="lang-cs prettyprint-override"><code>Form:
@using (Html.BeginForm(&quot;NewApplication&quot;, &quot;AppController&quot;, FormMethod.Post, new { id = &quot;AppForm&quot; }))
{ 
    &lt;button id=&quot;CreateButton&quot; type=&quot;submit&quot;&gt;Create&lt;/button&gt;
}
</code></pre>
<pre><code>JS: 
$(&quot;#AppForm&quot;).on(&quot;submit&quot;, function () {
    if ($(this).valid()) {
        $(&quot;#CreateButton&quot;).prop(&quot;disabled&quot;, true); 
        //Other stuff       
    }else{
        $(&quot;#CreateButton&quot;).prop(&quot;disabled&quot;, false);
        //Other stuff
    }
});
</code></pre>
<p>Instead of capturing button click. The submit button inside the mvc form when clicked will trigger the form submit event automatically. You can intercept that and check if form is valid or not and act accordingly.</p>
